cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this material, please cite it as below. Please also cite the original data sources listed in the README."
type: software
title: "Bioaccumulation in Aquatic Organisms: From One-Compartment Toxicokinetic Models to Real-World Complexity. Workshop material, University of Waterloo"
abstract: >-
  R scripts, curated datasets and teaching material for a half-day,
  hands-on workshop on toxicokinetic (TK) modelling of organic
  contaminants in aquatic invertebrates (University of Waterloo,
  12 November 2026). Exercises cover the one-compartment TK model,
  parent-metabolite (biotransformation) models, two-compartment models
  with receptor binding and lipid partitioning, and dietary uptake. The
  scripts are an R re-implementation of the BYOM model TK-metabolism and
  include the parameter-space explorer for confidence intervals.
